I have no particular interest in a non-Latin alphabet for Lojban
(learning the language *with* the Latin alphabet is hard enough for me),
but it would be interesting to have a *font* for Lojban that uses
ligatures for the consonant clusters and dipthongs.  This would give
written Lojban a bit of exotic flair without making it harder to read.

Of course, the language has *dozens* of consonant clusters, so making
such a font and making it look not-hideous would be a substantial
job...and if I had enough Copious Free Time to do such a thing, I would
spend more time *learning the damn language*...but as long as we're
musing about alphabets I thought I would put that idea on the table.


